The source in this repository is upstream faer plus tensor4all modifications.
The upstream copyright notice and the MIT text in LICENSE apply to it.
Except for explicitly identified ported material, modifications made in this
fork are Copyright (c) tensor4all contributors and are released under the same
MIT license.

LQ factorization, its factor extraction and the null-space blocks follow the
output conventions of MatrixAlgebraKit.jl (MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 Jutho
Haegeman and contributors, https://github.com/QuantumKitHub/MatrixAlgebraKit.jl,
commit 5120b5def1848d8ff63d80472aef8a290ddb60a6): the factor shapes, the trailing
null block of the full Q, and the real-nonnegative-diagonal gauge. The kernels
are faer's own and the decomposition is faer's blocked QR on the transposed view,
so no MatrixAlgebraKit expression is translated; MIT is the same license as this
repository's LICENSE and no additional COPYING file is required.

faer also contains code ported from other projects. Those files keep their own
terms and their notices ship alongside the crate:

  faer/COPYING.EIGEN.MPL2               divide-and-conquer SVD (Eigen)
  faer/COPYING.LAPACK.BSD               jacobi/givens, LLT full pivoting,
                                        column-pivoting QR, Schur, Hessenberg,
                                        Schur reordering, tridiagonal QR step,
                                        selected LAPACK EIG/LIN numerical validation tests
  faer/COPYING.BLAS.NETLIB              credit for the reference BLAS test programs
                                        whose BLAS-level checks the matmul,
                                        rank-update and triangular-solve unit tests
                                        adapt (docs/blas-test-inventory.md)
  faer/COPYING.SUITE_SPARSE.AMD.BSD     AMD ordering
  faer/COPYING.SUITE_SPARSE.COLAMD.BSD  COLAMD ordering

The faer package's `license = "MIT AND BSD-3-Clause"` metadata includes the
LAPACK numerical test adaptations. It does not relicense the other ported files;
read the COPYING files for their actual terms. The netlib reference BLAS test
programs ask for credit rather than imposing a license condition, and no Fortran
is translated: `faer/COPYING.BLAS.NETLIB` carries that credit and the quoted
notice, so the `license` expression stays as it is.

The packages published from this repository are the temporary tensor4all fork
names `t4a-faer` and `t4a-faer-traits`, so that downstream crates can depend on
fork content through crates.io, where a `git` dependency cannot be published.
Each published package carries a `LICENSE` copy; `faer` additionally carries the
COPYING files above.
